-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Inferno
  Publisher   Proxima Software, 1993
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Inferno.tzx
  MD5         335eec35a526f2044455cb87e8c77206

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Changes     1.1: Kempston joystick works; pilot SAVE and LOAD go to
              INFERNO.SAV on the SD card, with an autosave at each mission
              start; English briefing title pictures and attract-mode credits
              (MUSIC, GRAPHICS); no Czech flash before an English briefing.
              1.0: first NXC patch, from nexclash inferno hybrid build with
              English text; Czech as the language set

  Note        The whole game from the tape (intro, six levels, ending) with
              the figures as Next hardware sprites over a tilemap scenery; the
              original code runs, with small hooks for the joystick and the SD
              card saves. English is the default: the Language line steps
              English / Czech (the original text); the build is the same
              either way. English text is a reviewed translation of the Czech
              original (menus, intro, level briefings and their title
              pictures, story, debriefs, attract-mode credits, command words
              HELP KEY REP WEA QUI PAS). Needs a 2MB Next. Kempston joystick:
              answer Y (A in Czech) at the prompt; the stick moves and fires,
              weapon and activate stay on Symbol Shift and N. Pilots: the
              game's SAVE and LOAD use INFERNO.SAV in the game's folder on the
              SD card (up to 112 pilots, names matched in either case), and
              the pilot is saved by itself at the start of each mission; with
              no card the pilots stay in RAM. Do not run automap_fix or any
              DivMMC automap-off step on this build: the SD saves call esxDOS.

